  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Three places where tables live",
      "items": [
        "Pending Updates DB (one per region): firm_activation, engagement_index, engagement_events, template_versions, summaries_copy, work_items, processed_events",
        "Summaries DB (global, one instance): summaries, summary_provenance. No firm or engagement data",
        "outbox: recommended; one table added to the Product Template DB and one to each customer database",
        "summaries_copy holds copies of rows of summaries. It is not a foreign key: the two databases are not connected, the Reconciler asks the Summary Service"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What each table is",
      "items": [
        "engagement_events: source of truth and audit trail. Append-only, never updated or deleted. type is one of Registered, UpdateApplied, UpdateDeclined, OfferWithdrawn, Reconciled",
        "firm_activation: source of truth for the per-firm feature switch",
        "engagement_index: derived from engagement_events, one row per engagement, rebuildable",
        "template_versions: copy of the lineage, fed by TemplatePublished and TemplateWithdrawn, rebuildable",
        "summaries_copy: copy fetched by the Reconciler when a TemplatePublished arrives, or on demand if one is missing; rebuildable",
        "processed_events: makes the Reconciler idempotent and reveals sequence gaps",
        "work_items: the worker's work list and saga log, purgeable when a job ends",
        "work_items.trigger is activation, publish or sweep; work_items.status is pending, in_flight, done, failed or parked",
        "outbox.sent_at stays null until the broker acknowledges the event"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Rules the model encodes",
      "items": [
        "'Pending' is a query, not a table: engagement_index joined with template_versions",
        "summaries are immutable: a regenerated summary is a new row with a new id, the old one is kept",
        "summaries is unique on template_id + from_version + to_version + prompt_version",
        "outbox rows are written in the same transaction as the business change; the relay publishes rows whose sent_at is null",
        "source_event_id is unique in engagement_events, so the same incoming event cannot be recorded twice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Open points",
      "items": [
        "It is a proposal: columns and types are indicative, indexes are not defined",
        "It draws the event-sourced option (events are the truth, the index is a projection). The simpler option is still open: engagement_index as the truth and engagement_events only as an audit log",
        "The only identifiers of people or firms are firm_id and user_id. No engagement content is stored anywhere"
      ]
    }
  ]
